items.description:
Do you pride yourself on being the person who can actually find anything online? Then the Surfshark SEO team wants you.

We optimize Surfshark's website to bring in a steady flow of organic traffic across multiple search engines. Join us and you'll work at the intersection of tech, content, and localization — alongside on-site, off-page, and technical SEO specialists, content producers, copywriters, and web content specialists. If you're curious, inventive, and want a team that actually rewards those instincts, keep reading.

If you want to:

Drive organic growth through on-site SEO, with a focus on localized markets;
Spot and act on new SEO opportunities from competitor analysis, search trends, and keyword research;
Improve existing content with a data-driven, user-first approach;
Run content production, coordinating with writers, localization managers, and WP designers;
Monitor, analyze, and report on how our SEO is performing;
Experiment with AI Search optimization and make it work for us;
Sharpen workflows through automation;
Watch global SEO trends and find smart ways to put them to use.

And you can check off:

Proven experience of driving organic growth through smart SEO strategy;
A solid grasp of SEO best practices;
Confidence with SEO and analytics tools like Ahrefs and Google Search Console;
An eye for content that's both easy to read and built to rank;
An analytical, data-driven way of making decisions;
A habit of tracking AI Search developments and testing what actually works;
Clear communication and a collaborative streak;
Familiarity with international SEO and multilingual websites.

Here’s the deal:

Growth and learning opportunities: time dedicated to learning, conferences, online learning platforms, and books for your professional development;
Health and wellness: we want you to feel and be your best. That's why we offer various benefits, from online workouts, a physical coach and a gym to regular mental health checks;
Tools of your choice: choose technical equipment and the tools you need to do your best;
Community and celebrations: get ready for long-lasting traditions such as yearly workation, Friday get-togethers, various team buildings and company celebrations;
Convenient commuting: traveling from point A to point B can be a pain. That’s why, depending on your unique circumstances, we compensate part of your public transport costs;
Work-life balance: We encourage working in the office, with the possibility of up to two remote days per week. Plus, with our WFA policy, you can work from almost anywhere in the world;
Premium Surfshark accounts: for you, your family, and friends;
Gross salary: 2700-4150 Eur/month for the Lithuanian market, 10600-19400 Pln/month for the Polish market. It may vary depending on your skills and experience.
